==Points of Interest==
===Pokémon Fan Club===
On the west side of the city is a fan club for Pokémon. If the player listens to the club's chairman talk about his favorite Pokémon, they will receive a Bike Voucher which they can take to [[Cerulean City|Cerulean City's]] bike shop to redeem for a free Bicycle. There are also three NPCs in the fan club offering [[List of Gift Pokémon and Trades#NPC_Trades|trades]].

===Fishing Contest===
On the south coast of the city, to the east of the gym, is a daily fishing contest where the goal is to submit the heaviest Magikarp. The prize for winning the first time is a Magikarp Balaclava and an automatic hook which will automatically reel in anything the player finds while fishing. Any subsequent wins will be rewarded with ₽4,000.

The player can enter the contest by talking to the Fisherman with the blue vest jacket after obtaining any fishing rod. At the start of the contest, the player will be told the current heaviest Magikarp's weight, and the player can talk to the Fisherman again to check the weight of their own Magikarp, and the weight of the currently winning Magikarp. Each [[Time|in-game hour]], it is possible for another participant to have caught a heavier Magikarp. The competition ends at midnight, and the player must talk to the Fisherman in the blue vest jacket again to claim their prize.

A Magikarp's weight is determined by its IVs and its Level. Higher total IVs and Level mean a heavier Magikarp.<br/>
<math>{\text{Weight}} = \min(\max((10 \times (1 + \frac{{\text{IVs}}}{62} + \frac{{\text{Level}}}{200}))) - 10, 5), 40)</math><br/>
All other participant's Magikarps are calculated with a level of 5. If the player has not won the contest before, all other participant's Magikarp's weights will be reduced by 2kg after the normal weight calculation.

===Move Deleter===
On the east side of the city, next to the Hotel, is the Move Deleter. He is able to make any Pokémon forget any move for free.

===Rollout Move Tutor===
A Lass in the house to the east of the [[Route 6]] entrance will teach [[bulbapedia:Rollout (move)|Rollout]] to the player's Pokémon for {{P$}}2,000.

===Swift Move Tutor===
After completing the Seafood Cocktail [[Quests|quest]] on the upper floor of the hotel, the man will teach [[bulbapedia:Crabhammer (move)|Crabhammer]] to the player's Pokémon for free.

===Wonder Room Move Tutor===
A waiter in the Pokémon Center will teach [[bulbapedia:Wonder Room (move)|Wonder Room]] to the player's Pokémon for {{P$}}1,000.

===Balm Mushroom Collector===
The Pokémon Ranger on the ground floor of the hotel will purchase a {{ItemIcon|BALMMUSHROOM}} Balm Mushroom for {{P$}}15,000. This exchange can be repeated.

===Fighting Arena===
In the middle of the city is a construction site. After defeating the [[Elite Four]], the Fighting Arena will have been built. There the player will be able to have a [[Gym Leader rematches|rematch against any of the Gym Leaders]] with stronger teams.

